So you can tell by reading it, if I can't find an X here, I look in the enclosing block

03:10:17.540 --> 03:10:18.540
of code.

03:10:18.540 --> 03:10:25.579
I look in the enclosing block of source code, static scope.

03:10:25.579 --> 03:10:29.020
The compiler can figure it out.

03:10:29.020 --> 03:10:32.500
If you think about it this way, with dynamic scope,

03:10:32.500 --> 03:10:37.100
the compiler doesn't know what the call stack's

03:10:37.100 --> 03:10:40.299
going to look like at runtime, because the compiler

03:10:40.299 --> 03:10:42.559
is compiling the code and producing something

03:10:42.559 --> 03:10:44.860
that's executable.

03:10:44.860 --> 03:10:48.260
So that's why dynamic scope, whenever

03:10:48.260 --> 03:10:51.059
you hear the word dynamic, it's runtime.

03:10:51.059 --> 03:10:52.020
Runtime, dynamic.

03:10:52.020 --> 03:10:55.200
Dynamic runtime.

03:10:55.200 --> 03:10:57.840
That's an easy heuristic to remember that.

03:10:59.240 --> 03:11:00.800
